Z||000000||Greg Piet||09-10-1999||11:10 PM||||I just got one of those accelerometers which tells you your 0-60   60-0  1/4 mile, horsepower, and g's<P>I havent really played with it much in the car, but i did manage to go through the first 2 gears fully when trying to get my horsepower.  It was really low!  I did my best to meet the requirements, but I wasnt exactly on a track so conditions werent great.  Does anyone know the power curve for the v6?  what gear and rpm is supposed to be maximum hp?<P>Also if anyone else has used one of these, do they seem accurate?  it said it stopped calculating hp when one decelerated down to  30 mph, which is where it stopped so it appears at first glance to be fairly accurate.||||reg||5
Z||000001||Shaun41178||09-11-1999||02:15 AM||||Its amazing that this was posted today.  i just did a whole buch of qtr mile runs with my car today at the track and had the g-tech going as well to compare the times.  I will list track time and tehn g-tech time.<BR>Track-14.29@91.3....... G-14.32@95.3  NEW BEST!!<BR>Track-14.69@90.1....... G-14.50@95.3<BR>Track-14.40@90.8....... G-14.3@94.8<BR>Track-16.45@82.3....... G-16.2@86.4<BR>Track-14.66@89.6....... G-14.4@95.2<BR>Track-16.40@82.1....... G-16.1@86.1<P>The g-tech is pretty accurate with e.t.'s but is pretty off with mph.  Up to 5 mph in my case.  However it was only off .2 or so with the e.t's<P>I would say that it is accurate enough to give an idea of what your car can do.  It is accurate to 60.  not 100% accurate but really close to about a tenth or so.  <P>Oh yea I hit 5.6 to 60 tonight according to my g-tech.  That is my best so far.  Man I can't wait for my 3.2 rebuild to go in.  this car will run low 13's for sure<BR> <A HREF="http://members.aol.com/shaun41178" TARGET=_blank>http://members.aol.com/shaun41178</A>    thats my webpage in case anyone cares<BR>||||reg||12
Z||000002||Greg Piet||09-11-1999||03:12 AM||||I suppose that your little fiero isnt exactly stock?<P>I am very interested in the horsepower function which in my case really sucked 60 hp. I didnt follow the directions as I said i ony went through the first 2 gears, but I was on a public road and I didnt feel cozy cruising through downtown vegas trying to test it.  I forgot to ask what weight do others use for their vehicle (i am riding and 85 SE v-6 with AC)?<BR>The manual said take the gvwr and subtract 180 lbs for each passenger missing.  that would make the weight around 1500 lbs.  Is this right?<BR>I got my new "toy" last night so I havent really tried it out, but tomorrow im off to the racetrack, and that should help in getting more realistic numbers.  I am pretty sure I wont be pulling 14 sec 1/4 mile times though.<BR>Since I am in the process of doing a bit of upgrading, i wanted to  see the increase after each upgrade.||||reg||1
